{"type":"step-attempt","step":"spec-review","sessionId":"8257d94c-98b9-443d-a12f-69d93e30e0a5","outcome":{"verdict":"approved","findingsPath":"specrunner/changes/codex-scope-guidance/spec-review-result-001.md","error":null,"toolResult":{"ok":true,"approved":true,"findings":[{"severity":"low","resolution":"fixable","file":"specrunner/changes/codex-scope-guidance/tasks.md","title":"TC-012 (pure constant module invariant) has no dedicated runnable test task","rationale":"TC-012 ('scope-guidance.ts Is a Pure Constant Module with No Imports') is classified as category:unit / priority:should in test-cases.md. However, no task in T-01–T-05 creates an automated test that scans scope-guidance.ts itself for import declarations. T-05's guard test scans files OUTSIDE src/adapter/codex/, so it does not cover the module's own structure. T-01 acceptance criteria mentions 'no imports' but as a code-review check, not a runnable assertion. Since TC-012 is 'should' priority, the absence of an automated test does not block acceptance; a single file-scan assertion (following the dead-guidance.test.ts pattern) added to T-05 would close the gap."}],"evidence":{"checked":16,"skipped":3,"unverified":0},"observations":[{"severity":"low","file":"specrunner/changes/codex-scope-guidance/test-cases.md","title":"TC number reuse between new test-cases.md and existing test files","rationale":"TC-012 and TC-015 appear both in the new test-cases.md (for the codex-scope-guidance feature) and as labels in the pre-existing artifact-bundle-injection.test.ts. The design intentionally reuses TC-015 as a meta-requirement ('update old TC-015 to include guidance'), but globally the same number has two meanings. This is a readability note, not a correctness issue."},{"severity":"low","file":"specrunner/changes/codex-scope-guidance/test-cases.md","title":"TC-006 (should) and updated TC-015 (must) overlap in behavioral coverage","rationale":"TC-006's scenario ('no reportTool, no promptRules, no artifacts → prompt equals base+instructions+guidance') is satisfied by the T-04-updated TC-015 tests using toBe strict equality. There is no gap in coverage; the redundancy is intentional and harmless."},{"severity":"low","file":"specrunner/changes/codex-scope-guidance/spec.md","title":"Security: no surface exposed by this change","rationale":"The guidance text is a hardcoded ASCII constant with no user-supplied content. No auth, input-validation, or OWASP Top 10 concerns apply. The provider isolation (Codex adapter only) is enforced by the adapter boundary and the T-05 guard test."}]},"followUpAttempts":0,"transientRetryAttempts":0,"addedTurns":{"reportRetry":0,"postWork":0,"outputRepair":0}},"startedAt":"2026-08-26T11:48:42.832Z","endedAt":"2026-08-26T11:55:14.872Z","commitOid":"2dd16f9363e488100d504cce8439bd6689c99b27"}
