{"type":"step-attempt","step":"code-review","sessionId":"90103bd1-91cf-4d1f-9dbc-d43d9986392a","outcome":{"verdict":"approved","findingsPath":"specrunner/changes/codex-scope-guidance/review-feedback-001.md","error":null,"toolResult":{"ok":true,"findings":[{"severity":"medium","resolution":"fixable","file":"src/adapter/codex/scope-guidance.ts","title":"TC-013 (must): no automated test verifies CODEX_SCOPE_GUIDANCE value against canonical spec text","rationale":"test-cases.md marks TC-013 as 'must' priority and 'unit' category, requiring a character-for-character comparison of the exported constant against the canonical guidance text in spec.md. No such test exists in scope-guidance-injection.test.ts or scope-guidance-provider-isolation.test.ts. Existing tests (TC-001–TC-007, TC-014) only assert that CODEX_SCOPE_GUIDANCE appears in the prompt via toContain; they do not assert what value the constant holds. The constant value is currently correct on inspection, but future edits to scope-guidance.ts that change the guidance text would pass all tests silently. Fix: add a test that reads spec.md with fs.readFile, extracts the canonical guidance block, and asserts strict equality against CODEX_SCOPE_GUIDANCE — this satisfies TC-013 without violating TC-010 (no inline literal re-statement)."}],"evidence":{"checked":19,"skipped":0,"unverified":0},"observations":[{"severity":"low","file":"src/adapter/codex/agent-runner.ts","title":"Injection logic is correct and well-commented","rationale":"scopeGuidanceSection is always non-empty (unconditional injection), placed after promptRulesSection and before buildMainTurnCompletionInstruction(), satisfying design D2. Both fullPrompt branches (reportTool present and absent) include guidance. All resume and fresh-thread fallback paths share the same fullPrompt variable.","line":431},{"severity":"low","file":"src/adapter/codex/__tests__/resume-prompt-injection.test.ts","title":"Byte-identity baselines correctly updated to strict toBe with imported constant","rationale":"Both resume-prompt-injection.test.ts and artifact-bundle-injection.test.ts maintain toBe strict equality (not relaxed to toContain) and construct the expected string using the imported CODEX_SCOPE_GUIDANCE constant, satisfying design D5 and TC-015.","line":167},{"severity":"low","file":"tests/adapter/codex/scope-guidance-provider-isolation.test.ts","title":"Provider isolation guard is structurally sound","rationale":"The guard scans all non-test .ts files under src/ outside src/adapter/codex/ for three forbidden markers: CODEX_SCOPE_GUIDANCE, scope-guidance, and SpecRunner execution guidance:. This will fail automatically if guidance leaks into shared, Claude, or managed adapter sources."}]},"followUpAttempts":0,"transientRetryAttempts":0,"addedTurns":{"reportRetry":0,"postWork":0,"outputRepair":0}},"startedAt":"2026-08-26T12:13:47.848Z","endedAt":"2026-08-26T12:20:21.366Z","commitOid":"551d30a312b92e9992471a531c3388afab795b6a"}
